# Real employee contracts / personal documents used as reference material while
# building the document-templates module. These contain real personal data
# (names, addresses, dates of birth, RV-Nummer) and must never be committed --
# only structural field NAMES derived from them ever enter the repository.
Arbeitsvertrag*.pdf

# Ignored Sensitive Files
Arbeitsvertrag_Alona_Likhoto_final.pdf
hotelcrm-key1.pem


# Firebase Admin service-account keys, APNs signing keys, and anything derived
# from either. REAL SECRETS.
#
# The Firebase console's "Generate new private key" button downloads
# <project>-firebase-adminsdk-<hash>.json straight into whatever directory the
# browser last used -- frequently a repository root -- and a single
# `git add -A` would sweep it into a commit. That key grants full backend
# access to the Firebase project, Firestore included, bypassing
# firestore.rules entirely. A leak means rotating the key, not deleting the
# commit.
#
# The base64 forms are covered because the string in
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_BASE64 IS the private key, just re-encoded, and
# is no safer to commit than the JSON. *.p8 is the APNs signing key: same class
# of secret, arrives the same way.
#
# Nothing here ever needs to be tracked -- the backend reads the base64 from
# the environment, never a key file from disk.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
*service-account*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_BASE64*
*.p8
